    full_cli_phase3_root_process_exceeds_50g_during_hir_readoption_2026-11-22, 0, "2026-11-22 filed: f28 integ27 MemoryMax=50G OOM-killed at HIR adopt 3667/4139; stream or drop adopted HIR. See doc/08_tracking/bug/full_cli_phase3_root_process_exceeds_50g_during_hir_readoption_2026-11-22.md."
    full_cli_phase3_root_process_exceeds_50g_during_hir_readoption_2026-11-22, 1, "2026-11-27 Windows triage (release/1.0.0 7ec0a1ed579): status stays open. Verified PR #12199 (a948d0d1d99, stage2_cli_build_rss_cap_leak_check_closure_2026-11-27) updates shard_mem_clamp.spl and scripts/bootstrap/lib/product-frontend-policy.shs for MIR shard worker tree-cap admission (30 GiB/worker under 60 GiB cap), not a permanent code fix for root-process HIR re-adoption OOM. Operational Phase 4 mitigations recorded per lane handoff: #12199 + SIMPLE_MIR_SHARD_INTERFACE_HIR=1 + SIMPLE_STAGE3_STREAMING_SURFACES=1 (reported keeping interactive.spl at 10.56 GiB and Part B at ~8 GB/shard); permanent streaming/dropping of root-adopted HIR remains unverified on Windows (requires Linux Phase 3 Full-CLI build)."
